# Project

Canonical context: [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md). Read it before larger changes.
Detail: [docs/](../../docs/README.md); planned work: [specs/](../../specs/README.md).

Mobile-first, SEO-first booking site for an Agadir (Souss-Massa, Morocco) travel
agency: a static catalogue of 15 services across **excursions**, **activities**
and **transfers**, in **English and French** (Arabic planned, RTL). Next.js 16
App Router, React 19, TypeScript strict, next-intl, zod, Tailwind CSS v4, pnpm.

# Core rules

- Exactly one `<h1>`, one canonical and reciprocal `en`/`fr`/`x-default`
  hreflang, and valid JSON-LD per indexable page. `/book` is `noindex`.
- Never invent a price or duration; use `getServiceDisplayPrice` and
  `formatIsoDuration`. Never bypass the publish gate (`status: "published"`).
- UI copy lives in `messages/{en,fr}.json` via next-intl; service copy in
  `content/{en,fr}`. Do not hardcode user-visible strings.
- CSS logical properties only (`ms/me/ps/pe`, `start/end`, `text-start`).
- Keep dependencies tiny; ask before adding one.
- Leave the tree green: `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm test`, `pnpm build`.
  Add `pnpm test:e2e` when routes/metadata/i18n change.
- Never commit, push or open PRs unless asked.

# Commands

`pnpm dev`, `pnpm build`, `pnpm start`, `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`,
`pnpm test`, `pnpm test:e2e`, `pnpm validate:data`, `pnpm lighthouse`.
Use `corepack pnpm …`, or `node_modules/.bin/<tool>` when pnpm is unavailable.
